00:00:42.097 --> 00:00:49.257
Gross domestic product and personal consumption expenditures prints are competing with this week's Treasury supply for investor attention.

00:00:49.837 --> 00:00:54.337
And the Bank of Canada hike last week adds pressure on the same rate-sensitive sleeves.

00:00:54.337 --> 00:01:03.097
The S&amp;P 500 closed at 7,580, down 1.8% and the Toronto Stock Exchange Composite, or

00:01:03.097 --> 00:01:09.517
TSX Composite, closed at 35,620, down 1.7%.

00:01:09.517 --> 00:01:21.137
The NASDAQ Composite sits at 25,437, down 2.9%, up 9.47% year-to-date, and up 13.69% since

00:01:21.137 --> 00:01:24.717
the practice portfolio opened on March 16th, 2026.

00:01:25.517 --> 00:01:30.357
Earning season continues with multiple previews landing this week, so the tape is splitting

00:01:30.357 --> 00:01:34.137
attention between coupons, growth data, and company prints.

00:01:34.697 --> 00:01:41.317
About 25 days ago, we picked Broadcom, ticker AVGO, on an open AI chip catalyst that closed

00:01:41.317 --> 00:01:47.617
down 6.58%, a reminder that even strong narratives can stall when broader rotation hits.

00:01:47.617 --> 00:01:53.849
Dead issuance monitoring, using figures carried by unusual whales, is the weekly habit of

00:01:53.849 --> 00:01:57.509
reading gross treasury supply against the net cash actually raised.

00:01:58.029 --> 00:02:02.069
Then checking whether the high yield on the latest coupon sale is moving against you.

00:02:02.629 --> 00:02:06.769
Think of it like a bakery wheeling extra carts of bread onto the sidewalk at closing.

00:02:07.429 --> 00:02:12.149
The only way those extra loaves clear is if the price gets more tempting, and in bonds

00:02:12.149 --> 00:02:14.029
that temptation is a higher yield.

00:02:14.029 --> 00:02:19.709
This week's gross figure came across 11 sales of bills, floating rate notes, and notes

00:02:19.709 --> 00:02:26.889
due in 2, 5, and 7 years, eclipsing the prior record of $834 billion set a year earlier.

00:02:27.469 --> 00:02:34.909
Coupon sales alone totaled $213 billion, including $69 billion of 2-year notes, $70 billion

00:02:34.909 --> 00:02:38.109
of 5-year notes, and $44 billion of 7-year notes.

00:02:38.109 --> 00:02:44.749
The final seven-year tranche cleared at a high yield of 4.894%, with a bid to cover

00:02:44.749 --> 00:02:50.909
ratio of 2.46. Bid to cover is simply how many dollars of bids showed up for each dollar

00:02:50.909 --> 00:02:57.129
of notes for sale, so that 2.46 print tells you demand was there, but not at last sales

00:02:57.129 --> 00:03:03.309
yield. Only $106 billion represented net new cash after the balance rolled over maturing

00:03:03.309 --> 00:03:08.049
debt, far below the pandemic era weekly peak from March and April of 2020.

00:03:08.489 --> 00:03:14.209
You can screen this on Treasury Direct or Bloomberg Terminal, then compare that 7-year high yield

00:03:14.209 --> 00:03:18.969
against the prior sale to quantify the shift, which is the whole decision the technique is

00:03:18.969 --> 00:03:19.649
built to make.

00:03:20.149 --> 00:03:26.369
When bid to cover ratios rise above 2.4 while net issuance stays elevated, the technique flags

00:03:26.369 --> 00:03:32.089
potential headwinds for utilities and real estate investment trusts, or REITs in Canadian accounts.

00:03:32.089 --> 00:03:38.849
It worked in 2022 when repeated large auctions pushed 10-year yields above 4% and pressured

00:03:38.849 --> 00:03:40.169
dividend names for months.

00:03:40.749 --> 00:03:45.569
The risk appears when markets ignore supply because of flight to safety flows, as they

00:03:45.569 --> 00:03:51.889
did in early 2020 when net cash raised hit $362 billion a week, yet yields fell.

00:03:52.589 --> 00:03:57.449
Analyst Tony Fallon of Mischler Financial Group noted that the record-grows supply is not

00:03:57.449 --> 00:04:00.289
a good sign because investors may demand higher yields.

00:04:00.289 --> 00:04:06.149
roads. Run the screen weekly inside a tax-free savings account, or TFSA, or a registered

00:04:06.149 --> 00:04:12.009
retirement savings plan, or RRSP, by setting an alert for Treasury auction calendars and

00:04:12.009 --> 00:04:17.369
cross-checking the Netcash figure against the prior quarter average. Remember, gross supply

00:04:17.369 --> 00:04:23.929
is the weather report. Netcash is whether it actually rains. Hydro-1, ticker H on the TSX,

00:04:24.129 --> 00:04:28.769
is the simulated weekly hold, and this is a simulated trade for learning purposes with

00:04:28.769 --> 00:04:34.189
no real money. You see utilities under pressure after the hike and debt issuance monitoring

00:04:34.189 --> 00:04:39.909
already flags sector headwinds. Do you still take a regulated Ontario utility or do you

00:04:39.909 --> 00:04:44.989
wait for the yield dust to settle? Here's how I'd think about it. The technique keeps confidence

00:04:44.989 --> 00:04:49.769
at medium rather than high, and I used to treat a yield as permission to skip the stop,

00:04:50.309 --> 00:04:57.037
which is how an income story turns into an unplanned drawdown. Revenue rose 11% year over year to

00:04:57.037 --> 00:05:03.397
to $2.3 billion in the latest quarter, supported by approved rate increases and peak demand growth,

00:05:03.737 --> 00:05:08.317
while net profit climbed 13% year-over-year to $370 million.

00:05:09.037 --> 00:05:16.597
The stock trades near $55 Canadian dollars with a 2.6% yield and a market cap of $33.1 billion.

00:05:17.257 --> 00:05:22.677
A recent three-week rally places it above the 50-day average on the daily chart, while

00:05:22.677 --> 00:05:25.097
volume remains in line with the 20-day norm.

00:05:26.057 --> 00:05:34.417
Invalidation is an Ontario Energy Board rejection of the next major transmission filing, or a close below that 50-day moving average on the daily chart.

00:05:34.957 --> 00:05:38.117
That line is named before the simulated money is at risk.

00:05:38.637 --> 00:05:47.857
The stop loss sits 8% below entry, and caps the simulated loss at $80 on the $1,000 position if that invalidation level is reached.

00:05:47.857 --> 00:05:54.717
Target is plus 2% to plus 5% over the 5-session window, if rate-sensitive flows stabilize,

00:05:55.297 --> 00:06:00.217
and the hold enters at the next session's open, and is judged against the NASDAQ composite

00:06:00.217 --> 00:06:01.877
over those same 5 sessions.

00:06:02.397 --> 00:06:08.237
Confidence is medium, yield support, and essential service cash flows align, yet sector rotation

00:06:08.237 --> 00:06:10.097
signals remain mixed after the hike.

00:06:10.737 --> 00:06:16.437
Hydro-1 continues to invest in Ontario's electricity network, including applications for the roughly

00:06:16.437 --> 00:06:22.937
$1.9 billion northeast power line, and the $1.2 billion long wood to Lake Shore Transmission

00:06:22.937 --> 00:06:26.377
Line, which are earnings drivers distinct from bank holdings.

00:06:27.368 --> 00:06:31.688
Valuation discipline from the last closed hold is why the stop and the moving average

00:06:31.688 --> 00:06:36.408
and validation are written down first, rather than treating the yield as a reason to skip

00:06:36.408 --> 00:06:37.168
the exit rules.

00:06:37.708 --> 00:06:44.048
A five-session hold in power corporation of Canada, ticker POW, was the last weekly hold,

00:06:44.048 --> 00:06:49.568
A simulated buy at the Monday open that we exited at Friday's close on October 30th,

00:06:49.568 --> 00:06:50.388
2026.

00:06:51.228 --> 00:06:53.968
Entry was $92.91 Canadian.

00:06:54.548 --> 00:07:04.048
Exit was $96.60, a gain of $3.97% or $39.72 on the $1,000 position.

00:07:04.748 --> 00:07:11.168
The NASDAQ composite over those same sessions fell 2.27%, so the trade's alpha was plus

00:07:11.168 --> 00:07:12.928
6.24%.

00:07:12.928 --> 00:07:14.908
Stated confidence was medium.

00:07:15.388 --> 00:07:21.108
Stated invalidation was quarterly net income growth falling below 5%, or a close below

00:07:21.108 --> 00:07:24.948
the 50-day moving average on the daily chart, and it never triggered.

00:07:25.508 --> 00:07:27.948
The stated stop below entry was not reached.

00:07:28.448 --> 00:07:33.028
The medium grade matched the mixed setup of earnings visibility against rotation pressure,

00:07:33.448 --> 00:07:38.188
and the invalidation level worked as a guardrail even while the index moved against the name.

